WEBVTT

01:40.060 --> 01:41.860
These next few days,

01:41.900 --> 01:44.540
you guys are all heading off to college.

01:44.580 --> 01:45.960
So today,

01:46.000 --> 01:47.500
our families got together

01:47.540 --> 01:50.440
to throw you a little send-off.

01:50.980 --> 01:52.800
And, well,

01:52.840 --> 01:54.740
since you're all 18 now,

01:54.780 --> 01:57.160
you're officially allowed
a little sip of alcohol.

01:58.000 --> 01:59.360
- Really?
- Dad…

01:59.400 --> 02:01.080
We're students. No drinking for us.

02:01.580 --> 02:03.040
Don't think I don't know who's been

02:03.080 --> 02:04.780
dipping into that bottle of Wuliangye

02:04.820 --> 02:05.660
in the cabinet.

02:05.700 --> 02:06.840
Isn't it you guys' doing?

02:06.880 --> 02:07.880
Come on, fess up.

02:07.920 --> 02:09.060
How did he find out?

02:09.100 --> 02:10.960
- They drink it?
- Did they?

02:11.000 --> 02:13.480
- These kids.
- Fangyuan, come on, pour everyone a glass.

02:15.420 --> 02:16.260
Do you want one?

02:16.300 --> 02:17.600
Pour it up.

02:17.640 --> 02:18.520
Pour me one too.

02:18.560 --> 02:20.340
Forget it.
If you don't wanna smile, don't.

02:20.380 --> 02:21.440
Let's have a drink.

02:21.480 --> 02:23.280
- …yeah, that'll do.
- Wait.

02:23.320 --> 02:24.340
Where's your amber necklace?

02:24.380 --> 02:25.360
You're not wearing it.

02:25.400 --> 02:27.480
We are not having that in normal days.

02:27.520 --> 02:29.380
- Can I have a sip?
- Today, let's…

02:29.420 --> 02:32.540
It disappeared right after
Jiang Qiaoxi came back

02:32.580 --> 02:33.500
last time.

02:33.540 --> 02:35.560
Here…

02:35.600 --> 02:36.840
Come on now, kids.

02:36.880 --> 02:37.760
Listen up.

02:37.800 --> 02:38.980
I know

02:39.020 --> 02:40.560
you've snuck drinks before,

02:40.600 --> 02:42.840
but you don't actually
know how to drink yet.

02:42.880 --> 02:43.720
Let me show you.

02:44.500 --> 02:45.900
When you drink,

02:45.940 --> 02:47.840
hold the glass with your right hand,

02:48.520 --> 02:49.960
support the base with your left.

02:50.500 --> 02:51.780
When you toast someone,

02:51.820 --> 02:53.200
make sure your glass

02:53.240 --> 02:54.800
is a little lower than theirs.

02:54.840 --> 02:56.200
You know why?

02:56.240 --> 02:58.220
It shows respect.

02:58.260 --> 02:59.720
Respect. Respect!

02:59.760 --> 03:01.020
- Respect…
- No no, please.

03:01.060 --> 03:02.680
- I should be respecting you.
- Come on, cheers.

03:02.720 --> 03:04.200
- Let's all drink together.
- Cheers.

03:04.240 --> 03:05.180
- Happy days.
- Cheers.

03:05.220 --> 03:06.320
Cheers.

03:09.500 --> 03:10.880
You drank it all?

03:10.920 --> 03:11.940
Yu Qiao.

03:12.900 --> 03:14.500
Yun, Yingtao, listen up.

03:14.540 --> 03:16.840
When you're out there,
you can't drink at will.

03:16.880 --> 03:18.600
Especially you girls.

03:18.640 --> 03:20.860
No matter what happens,
don't let yourselves get drunk.

03:20.900 --> 03:21.880
Got it?

03:21.920 --> 03:23.480
- When have you ever seen
- Got it.

03:23.520 --> 03:24.360
my daughter drink?

03:24.400 --> 03:25.900
Uncle Cai, we hear you.

03:25.940 --> 03:26.920
If anyone's getting drunk,

03:26.960 --> 03:28.600
it's whoever tries to keep up
with Qin Yeyun.

03:31.640 --> 03:34.020
- He's kidding. Just jokes.
- Oh, jokes.

03:34.060 --> 03:35.980
Once you're out there on your own,

03:36.700 --> 03:38.860
you'll have to rely on yourselves.

03:38.900 --> 03:40.080
You've got to learn

03:40.120 --> 03:42.160
to keep your eyes open and ears sharp.

03:42.200 --> 03:43.420
When you run into trouble,

03:43.460 --> 03:45.340
use your head. Think it through.

03:46.140 --> 03:48.280
If it's tough, try to push through.

03:49.420 --> 03:50.860
And if you can't,

03:52.140 --> 03:53.300
come home

03:53.340 --> 03:54.520
and talk to us.

04:03.260 --> 04:04.800
That's, um, that's all I've got.

04:05.760 --> 04:07.740
You guys say something.

04:08.280 --> 04:09.680
Say a few words.

04:10.380 --> 04:12.040
Alright, I'll say a little.

04:12.080 --> 04:14.580
All I hope is you

04:15.600 --> 04:18.680
eat well, sleep well, and study well.

04:18.720 --> 04:20.060
Try to be one of those

04:20.100 --> 04:21.440
Model Students, okay?

04:22.280 --> 04:23.120
And don't worry

04:23.720 --> 04:24.820
about things back home.

04:27.240 --> 04:28.500
We've got it covered.

04:28.540 --> 04:29.860
That's me. I'm done.

04:33.140 --> 04:33.980
Here.

04:37.260 --> 04:39.820
Every person is born with a purpose.

04:39.860 --> 04:42.220
Raise your sails and ride the waves.

04:42.880 --> 04:44.620
I wish you all

04:44.660 --> 04:45.560
a bright future.

04:50.380 --> 04:51.220
Thank you.

04:53.280 --> 04:54.340
My turn.

04:54.380 --> 04:55.880
You're making this way too serious.

04:55.920 --> 04:56.980
Go on, go on.

05:01.240 --> 05:02.080
Your dad's stepping up.

05:06.220 --> 05:08.720
I don't usually talk much,

05:08.760 --> 05:10.260
but today I have to say something.

05:11.880 --> 05:13.100
From now on,

05:13.140 --> 05:15.560
you've got to take care of yourselves.
Live your own lives.

05:15.600 --> 05:17.860
Of course, I hope everything you run into

05:17.900 --> 05:19.340
will be good things,

05:19.380 --> 05:21.580
nothing bad at all.

05:21.620 --> 05:22.980
But think about it.

05:23.020 --> 05:24.780
How could anyone

05:24.820 --> 05:25.960
go through life

05:26.000 --> 05:27.900
with only good things happening?

05:28.760 --> 05:30.700
There's no way you can get through it

05:30.740 --> 05:31.860
without hurtful things,

05:31.900 --> 05:33.200
without something

05:33.240 --> 05:34.700
that breaks your heart.

05:34.740 --> 05:35.580
Right?

05:36.080 --> 05:37.440
So remember this.

05:37.480 --> 05:39.760
Whatever pain you're feeling right now,

05:39.800 --> 05:41.220
it'll pass.

05:41.260 --> 05:42.980
Even the bad things

05:43.020 --> 05:45.700
can turn into something good, eventually.

05:47.260 --> 05:48.860
And one last thing. Someone once said,

05:49.360 --> 05:51.880
when you wade through
the river of your life,

05:51.920 --> 05:54.700
every bit of joy and pain you feel

05:55.200 --> 05:58.480
will become part of the scenery.

05:58.520 --> 06:01.180
And you are the best part of it.

06:01.220 --> 06:02.100
Well said!

06:02.640 --> 06:03.760
Beautifully said.

06:03.800 --> 06:04.820
So good.

06:08.420 --> 06:09.320
Alright. Now is time

06:09.360 --> 06:11.300
for a word from the moms.

06:11.340 --> 06:13.220
- Baoxuan. Say something.
- Come on.

06:14.060 --> 06:15.600
What would I even say?

06:15.640 --> 06:16.760
Feels kinda cheesy.

06:17.400 --> 06:18.360
I'll pass.

06:19.480 --> 06:20.400
Be safe out there.

06:20.440 --> 06:22.080
- Thank you.
- Hey, come on.

06:22.120 --> 06:23.480
Why are you crying?

06:23.520 --> 06:25.180
It's a happy day, remember?

06:25.220 --> 06:26.060
Yeah, happy.

06:28.220 --> 06:30.420
Are we being too loud?
Maybe we're disturbing the neighbors.

06:31.040 --> 06:32.680
- Maybe.
- I'll get the door. I'll get it.

06:32.720 --> 06:34.640
Yingtao, your surprise is here.

06:34.680 --> 06:35.720
Wait for it.

06:36.460 --> 06:37.520
Surprise?

06:38.180 --> 06:39.140
What surprise?

06:39.820 --> 06:40.800
Jiang Qiaoxi?

06:42.740 --> 06:43.600
Hello.

06:47.240 --> 06:48.540
You are…

06:48.580 --> 06:50.920
Come in, come in. Don't block the doorway.

06:52.600 --> 06:53.860
- Is he…?
- Yingtao.

06:54.360 --> 06:56.520
You don't remember Chen Minghao?

06:57.680 --> 07:00.200
Look how grown up you are now, Yingtao!

07:00.240 --> 07:02.040
Chen Minghao?

07:02.080 --> 07:03.320
Hello, Aunties and Uncles.

07:03.820 --> 07:05.560
- Hello!
- Sit.

07:05.600 --> 07:06.520
- Have a seat.
- Come.

07:06.560 --> 07:07.480
- Come.
- Sit.

07:07.520 --> 07:09.580
You brought so many gifts too?

07:09.620 --> 07:10.800
Minghao,

07:10.840 --> 07:12.340
how are your parents?

07:12.380 --> 07:14.620
They're doing well. Just super busy.

07:14.660 --> 07:16.400
Otherwise, they would've come with me.

07:17.100 --> 07:18.340
They're always saying

07:18.380 --> 07:21.500
Uncle Cai and Auntie Kang
took such good care of my grandparents.

07:21.540 --> 07:22.820
Since I finally came back,

07:22.860 --> 07:24.440
they insisted I come visit.

07:24.480 --> 07:26.900
We're all neighbors from back in the day.
No need to be so formal.

07:26.940 --> 07:28.360
Your grandma was always

07:28.400 --> 07:29.660
looking out for us.

07:29.700 --> 07:31.520
She'd share anything good she had with us.

07:32.140 --> 07:34.360
Where are you studying abroad, Minghao?

07:34.860 --> 07:36.240
Australia, Uncle Yu.

07:37.500 --> 07:38.700
Australia?

07:39.200 --> 07:41.020
That must cost a fortune

07:41.060 --> 07:42.340
to study there.

07:42.960 --> 07:45.980
Well, it really depends
on the universities and the location.

07:46.020 --> 07:47.960
The costs can vary a lot.

07:48.500 --> 07:49.840
Yun could do her undergrad here

07:49.880 --> 07:51.620
and apply for grad school in Australia.

07:53.440 --> 07:55.540
Dad, stop daydreaming.

07:55.580 --> 07:57.540
School's school.
Don't care about going abroad.

07:59.940 --> 08:01.160
Minghao,

08:01.960 --> 08:03.560
have you been living alone

08:03.600 --> 08:04.980
all these years?

08:05.020 --> 08:06.120
Yeah, just me.

08:06.160 --> 08:08.400
It it hard being abroad on your own?

08:09.080 --> 08:10.780
Was it easy to find food?

08:10.820 --> 08:12.140
Did you make any friends?

08:12.920 --> 08:16.960
Is it tough speaking
another language all the time?

08:17.000 --> 08:18.580
I manage okay.

08:18.620 --> 08:21.120
But those who work while studying
really have it rough.

08:21.160 --> 08:24.280
Classes during the day,
waiting tables at night.

08:24.320 --> 08:26.860
My parents don't allow me to work at all.

08:27.360 --> 08:29.520
They say if I'm there to study,
then I should just focus.

08:29.560 --> 08:31.760
They even rented me a place off-campus.

08:31.800 --> 08:33.640
On weekends I can
throw parties with friends.

08:33.679 --> 08:34.720
Can't complain.

08:35.299 --> 08:36.659
Your parents are so nice.

08:37.679 --> 08:38.640
Yingtao,

08:38.679 --> 08:41.340
I heard you got into
Northern Normal University.

08:41.980 --> 08:43.320
You used to be that sweet little girl

08:43.360 --> 08:45.080
with the red bead necklace

08:45.120 --> 08:46.580
always chasing after me.

08:46.620 --> 08:48.280
Now you're headed to a top university.

08:48.780 --> 08:49.840
That's amazing.

08:50.860 --> 08:51.940
Thanks.

08:52.440 --> 08:55.160
But it wasn't a red bead.

08:55.200 --> 08:56.300
It was amber.

08:56.340 --> 08:59.140
Oh! My bad. Sorry about that.

08:59.180 --> 09:00.740
Minghao, eat more.

09:03.380 --> 09:04.780
Come on, everyone, dig in.

09:04.820 --> 09:05.660
Here, help yourself.

09:06.600 --> 09:08.120
Alright. You guys can head back.

09:08.160 --> 09:09.500
- Bye-bye.
- See you, Minghao.

09:10.260 --> 09:11.260
Take care!

09:12.160 --> 09:13.100
- Bye!
- Bye!

09:13.140 --> 09:14.200
Bye-bye!

09:17.480 --> 09:19.960
Why'd you suddenly bring Minghao here?

09:20.920 --> 09:23.320
That was your big surprise
for Lin Yingtao?

09:23.360 --> 09:25.440
Du Shang, come on. You explain

09:25.480 --> 09:27.740
why we set this whole thing up.

09:28.920 --> 09:29.880
Yingtao.

09:30.660 --> 09:31.640
Have you really forgotten?

09:31.680 --> 09:33.840
Back when we all saw Minghao off,

09:33.880 --> 09:35.160
you cried

09:35.200 --> 09:36.560
like the world was ending.

09:37.060 --> 09:38.100
You cried so hard,

09:38.140 --> 09:40.060
it felt like the whole town
could hear you.

09:40.700 --> 09:42.820
But look at today.
You barely even recognized him.

09:42.860 --> 09:44.300
So yeah,

09:44.340 --> 09:46.480
get ready to soak up
the whole college experience.

09:47.580 --> 09:48.660
Because one day,

09:49.160 --> 09:50.620
when you think about that person,

09:50.660 --> 09:52.200
you might feel just like this.

09:55.420 --> 09:56.440
Really?

09:56.480 --> 09:57.580
Of course.

10:01.960 --> 10:03.880
But that person is Jiang Qiaoxi.

10:05.980 --> 10:07.520
- What?
- You two

10:07.560 --> 10:09.220
really think you're geniuses, huh?

10:10.780 --> 10:11.960
Wait…

10:12.000 --> 10:14.280
- We didn't do anything wrong.
- What do you mean?

10:14.320 --> 10:15.660
Can't you see she's upset?

10:15.700 --> 10:17.240
Why'd you rush off like that?

10:20.820 --> 10:22.180
I was just thinking,

10:23.360 --> 10:24.900
if Jiang Qiaoxi hadn't been around,

10:25.720 --> 10:26.560
I probably

10:26.600 --> 10:28.340
wouldn't have worked so hard
in middle school.

10:28.880 --> 10:30.800
Wouldn't have gotten
into Experimental High,

10:31.360 --> 10:32.980
Wouldn't have made it to Northern Normal.

10:34.460 --> 10:35.760
That came out of nowhere.

10:35.800 --> 10:37.360
Bit of a sharp turn there.

10:41.020 --> 10:42.360
I had to say it while I remembered.

10:45.460 --> 10:46.500
Where is he now anyway?

10:49.400 --> 10:50.320
No idea.

10:52.680 --> 10:53.660
It's alright.

10:53.700 --> 10:55.200
I'll help you find out.

10:55.240 --> 10:56.200
I mean, he still

10:57.160 --> 10:58.120
has to go to college.

10:59.720 --> 11:01.140
We'll hear from him eventually.

11:04.500 --> 11:05.480
I think so too.

11:08.640 --> 11:10.820
By the way, Lin Yingtao,

11:11.320 --> 11:14.520
Northern Aviation and Northern Normal
are barely three kilometers apart.

11:14.560 --> 11:16.060
We're even registering just a day apart.

11:16.100 --> 11:17.940
So why don't you want to go together?

11:19.520 --> 11:21.880
I just wanted to see what it feels like

11:21.920 --> 11:25.420
leaving home completely on my own

11:25.460 --> 11:26.980
and stepping into something new.

11:49.420 --> 11:50.440
Yingtao,

11:51.180 --> 11:53.060
I think Jiang Qiaoxi's kind of

11:53.560 --> 11:54.700
a jerk.

11:56.420 --> 11:57.640
Look at him.

11:57.680 --> 11:59.300
Before he left for Hong Kong,

11:59.340 --> 12:02.060
he gave you lipstick and red heels.

12:02.620 --> 12:05.120
Once you turn 18,
you're not just a girl anymore.

12:05.160 --> 12:07.200
You're starting to become a woman.

12:07.240 --> 12:09.460
And lipstick and heels?
That's a woman's starter kit.

12:09.500 --> 12:11.800
He gave those to you
so he'd always have a claim

12:11.840 --> 12:13.080
on that part of you.

12:20.540 --> 12:21.680
Total jerk move.

12:22.220 --> 12:25.180
Yeah, he did it so you'd never forget him.

12:26.360 --> 12:29.120
Guy's a math genius.
He knows exactly what he's doing.

12:33.420 --> 12:34.400
Yingtao,

12:35.060 --> 12:36.620
don't forget about me.

12:39.320 --> 12:41.320
Why is it everyone wants me to forget him?

12:44.960 --> 12:46.660
Because we just want you to be okay.

12:48.720 --> 12:50.060
He'll come back.

12:51.080 --> 12:52.120
When?

12:58.860 --> 13:01.540
You're going to Hongyang with Yu Qiao.

13:01.580 --> 13:03.380
Let him take you out, hang out more.

13:03.920 --> 13:05.300
He's actually a good guy.

13:06.000 --> 13:07.200
Better than Jiang Qiaoxi.

13:11.160 --> 13:12.560
What are you talking about?

13:14.340 --> 13:15.620
I'm just saying,

13:16.120 --> 13:18.300
Yu Qiao's gonna be a pilot.
Once he's in uniform,

13:18.340 --> 13:20.180
he'll be swimming in admirers.

13:20.760 --> 13:22.800
No sense letting someone else have it.

13:22.840 --> 13:24.780
Better he is with you and
stay in the family.

13:27.100 --> 13:28.820
Can you stop with the nonsense?

13:30.240 --> 13:32.200
You don't need to worry about me.

13:32.240 --> 13:34.760
Looking like this? Once I get to college,
I'll have plenty of options.

13:35.780 --> 13:36.960
Guys who treats me right,

13:37.000 --> 13:39.320
buys me heels and lipstick?

13:39.360 --> 13:41.000
That's nothing.

13:43.660 --> 13:45.600
But look at you.

13:45.640 --> 13:47.800
Aside from your grades
being better than mine,

13:48.460 --> 13:51.820
your looks, your body, your brains,

13:51.860 --> 13:54.260
and your EQ

13:55.120 --> 13:56.400
are pretty average.

13:58.700 --> 14:01.480
Why are you staying in my room
and insulting me?

14:02.460 --> 14:03.540
Why are you mouthing off?

14:04.040 --> 14:04.940
Get out of my bed.

14:04.980 --> 14:06.760
Go sleep in your own.

14:06.800 --> 14:09.900
Because you're really
getting on my nerves.

14:12.700 --> 14:14.460
Alright, alright, I surrender.

14:15.900 --> 14:17.140
I'm sorry.

14:27.140 --> 14:28.180
Qin Yeyun…

14:31.780 --> 14:33.000
This time,

14:34.480 --> 14:35.820
it's just you staying.

14:36.440 --> 14:37.820
The rest of us are all leaving.

14:39.000 --> 14:40.100
Are you gonna be sad?

14:41.800 --> 14:43.080
You're all leaving,

14:43.120 --> 14:44.100
but I'm staying.

14:44.140 --> 14:45.420
You should be the ones feeling bad.

14:47.200 --> 14:48.700
You know what?

14:48.740 --> 14:50.120
You're getting on my nerves, too.

14:52.560 --> 14:53.540
You've always

14:54.040 --> 14:57.080
acted like nothing gets to you,
like you don't care about anything.

14:58.420 --> 14:59.680
But that just

15:00.740 --> 15:02.320
makes us worry about you more.

15:06.640 --> 15:07.620
Let's get some sleep.

15:08.120 --> 15:09.500
You've got a long trip tomorrow.

15:31.800 --> 15:32.920
I don't think

15:36.720 --> 15:39.160
I'll ever like someone this much again.

15:42.680 --> 15:43.760
You're only 18.

15:44.500 --> 15:45.500
Don't go saying ever.

16:08.120 --> 16:11.120
Jiang Qiaoxi, when you get to the city,

16:11.160 --> 16:12.620
will you call me?

16:13.660 --> 16:14.840
I will.

16:14.880 --> 16:17.280
Liar. You never did.

16:26.080 --> 16:28.900
Yingtao, I'm sorry.

16:42.580 --> 16:43.420
Jiang Qiaoxi!

16:45.420 --> 16:46.600
Jiang Qiaoxi!

16:46.640 --> 16:47.840
Where did you go?

16:48.520 --> 16:49.660
Come back!

16:51.280 --> 16:53.280
I'm serious! My memory's not that great.

16:53.320 --> 16:55.320
I really will forget you!

16:56.920 --> 16:58.180
Jiang Qiaoxi!

17:12.780 --> 17:16.760
NORTHERN NORMAL UNIVERSITY

17:16.800 --> 17:21.740
INNOVATION AND KNOWLEDGE SHAPE THE FUTURE
TOGETHER WE BUILD A SMART CAMPUS

17:21.780 --> 17:23.680
WELCOME NEW STUDENTS,
REGISTRATION SERVICES

17:30.600 --> 17:34.040
2008 INCOMING FEMALE DORM ASSIGNMENTS

17:42.500 --> 17:45.520
FOUR-YEAR PLAN: FRESHMAN FOCUS
01 ADAPT TO CAMPUS LIFE 02 FIND YOUR PATH

17:45.560 --> 17:48.420
SET SAIL FOR YOUR FUTURE
WELCOME NEW STUDENTS

17:53.660 --> 17:55.800
Okay, next. You are done.

17:57.000 --> 17:57.980
Come here.

17:59.800 --> 18:01.460
Here, look at the camera.

18:02.120 --> 18:04.040
Chin down a bit. There.

18:29.460 --> 18:30.580
Is this the one?

18:35.860 --> 18:37.940
Should be a little further up.

19:03.440 --> 19:04.420
Who is it?

19:05.140 --> 19:06.480
Oh, sorry, seniors.

19:08.060 --> 19:11.820
Hi, I'm Lin Qile,
class of 2008, elementary education major.

19:11.860 --> 19:12.700
Hi, seniors.

19:13.240 --> 19:14.600
Sorry if I woke you.

19:15.440 --> 19:17.180
- Sorry.
- Could you turn the lights on?

19:30.720 --> 19:32.120
Get up, get up, come on.

19:36.760 --> 19:38.140
It's fine, I got it.

19:39.300 --> 19:40.440
Can you help me carry this?

19:40.480 --> 19:41.880
This thing is so heavy,

19:41.920 --> 19:43.320
and you want me to carry it?

19:44.160 --> 19:45.240
Whose is this?

19:46.720 --> 19:47.820
I'll put it down for you.

19:48.460 --> 19:50.780
- You put them away then.
- Put away what?

19:50.820 --> 19:51.900
Scoot.

19:52.400 --> 19:53.680
Where are you from?

19:53.720 --> 19:56.240
I'm from Jialin.

19:56.960 --> 19:58.760
- I will put it here, okay?
- I brought some

19:58.800 --> 20:00.860
local snacks from home for everyone.

20:01.820 --> 20:04.160
Whose is this? You spilled it everywhere.

20:04.900 --> 20:06.120
Who left it here? Meng Lijun?

20:06.160 --> 20:09.060
Alright, alright, quit bickering,
you two. It's annoying.

20:09.100 --> 20:10.860
Take a seat, don't rush.

20:12.640 --> 20:15.080
Wait, why are you rooming with seniors?

20:15.900 --> 20:17.700
Can you ask the counselor to switch you?

20:17.740 --> 20:20.100
It's better to be
with your own classmates.

20:20.140 --> 20:22.060
You'll get to know each other faster.

20:22.100 --> 20:23.800
Plus, seniors are way older.

20:23.840 --> 20:25.280
You might not even get along.

20:26.000 --> 20:27.000
It's fine.

20:27.840 --> 20:30.460
Rooming with seniors

20:30.960 --> 20:32.020
could be a good thing.

20:32.060 --> 20:33.880
If I run into any academic stuff,

20:33.920 --> 20:35.540
I can ask them for help.

20:35.580 --> 20:37.020
Exactly. Good point.

20:37.060 --> 20:38.740
Just settle in and get along
with your seniors.

20:38.780 --> 20:40.460
Be proactive, stay open.

20:40.500 --> 20:41.980
If you feel overwhelmed,

20:42.020 --> 20:43.020
just call us.

20:43.520 --> 20:44.700
Got it.

20:44.740 --> 20:45.720
Yingtao, wait.

20:45.760 --> 20:47.100
Did you buy your bedding yet?

20:47.140 --> 20:48.760
The comforter insert, you know,

20:48.800 --> 20:50.140
the thing inside the blanket.

20:50.180 --> 20:51.200
Get a good one.

20:51.240 --> 20:52.260
The quality matters.

20:52.300 --> 20:53.940
Check the cotton inside. Don't buy it

20:53.980 --> 20:55.120
if it's dark or clumpy.

20:55.160 --> 20:56.220
And your pillow.

20:56.260 --> 20:58.140
Get one that's a little firm.

20:58.180 --> 20:59.340
It's better for your neck.

20:59.380 --> 21:00.240
Also,

21:00.280 --> 21:02.560
that first glass of water
in the morning is important.

21:02.600 --> 21:04.360
It flushes out toxins
and rehydrates your body.

21:04.400 --> 21:05.400
Have your glass of water.

21:06.080 --> 21:07.920
Did you hear what your mom just said?

21:08.580 --> 21:09.720
Mm, she's got it memorized.

21:09.760 --> 21:10.720
You've said it many times.

21:10.760 --> 21:13.200
Well, I used to
pour her morning water for her.

21:13.240 --> 21:14.600
If I don't nag her,

21:14.640 --> 21:15.960
she won't take it seriously.

21:16.000 --> 21:18.120
She knows. She's not a kid anymore.

21:18.160 --> 21:20.520
Only because you always beat me to it.

21:20.560 --> 21:22.140
I didn't get the chance to pour it myself.

21:23.060 --> 21:23.980
Alright, I get it.

21:24.020 --> 21:26.140
You don't have to worry so much.
I'll be fine.

21:26.180 --> 21:29.980
I've got training at the freshman
bootcamp this afternoon.

21:30.020 --> 21:31.200
I'm gonna go pack now.

21:31.860 --> 21:33.520
Okay then, that's it for now.

21:33.560 --> 21:34.560
Stay safe, okay?

21:34.600 --> 21:36.180
- Alright, talk later.
- Bye.

21:50.820 --> 21:52.500
Eyes right!

21:53.440 --> 21:54.640
Tiny steps!

21:54.680 --> 21:55.700
Eyes forward!

21:56.400 --> 21:57.240
At ease!

21:58.200 --> 21:59.320
Attention!

22:01.240 --> 22:02.320
Now, follow my lead.

22:03.140 --> 22:04.800
Left turn!

22:06.860 --> 22:07.760
Don't move.

22:07.800 --> 22:08.700
Who told you to move?

22:10.040 --> 22:11.320
What's wrong with you?

22:11.360 --> 22:13.500
Sir, I feel dizzy.

22:13.540 --> 22:15.140
Not just trying to get out of training?

22:15.180 --> 22:17.240
I haven't been feeling well.

22:17.280 --> 22:19.300
I've had a splitting headache
for two days.

22:19.340 --> 22:20.200
Someone help her out.

22:20.740 --> 22:21.660
Step forward.

22:22.400 --> 22:24.080
Take her to the infirmary for a check-up.

22:25.180 --> 22:26.600
- The rest of you,
- You good?

22:27.100 --> 22:28.080
follow my lead.

22:29.000 --> 22:30.320
Right turn!

22:31.320 --> 22:33.280
- Hang in there, we're almost
- Left turn!

22:33.320 --> 22:34.520
at the infirmary.

22:35.300 --> 22:36.960
- Move faster.
- Slow down, careful.

22:37.000 --> 22:37.940
Right turn!

22:37.980 --> 22:39.200
Slower, careful.

22:40.300 --> 22:42.820
Not bad. Let's go again. Follow my lead.

22:42.860 --> 22:44.520
About face!

22:46.220 --> 22:47.620
Let's head back to the dorms.

22:49.480 --> 22:50.320
You good now?

22:50.360 --> 22:53.280
I said I'm dizzy, aren't you dizzy too?

22:54.560 --> 22:56.020
I'm not dizzy.

22:57.180 --> 22:58.540
Hold your position.

22:58.580 --> 23:00.280
I'm really dizzy. I swear.

23:00.780 --> 23:02.240
You're seriously not dizzy?

23:08.340 --> 23:09.260
Move faster.

23:10.900 --> 23:12.200
Come on, pick it up.

23:13.040 --> 23:14.740
Eyes forward!

23:16.120 --> 23:17.260
Eyes right!

23:17.840 --> 23:19.040
Eyes front!

23:19.640 --> 23:20.660
Sir!

23:20.700 --> 23:21.740
I'm back.

23:21.780 --> 23:22.660
Fall in.

23:25.640 --> 23:26.520
Everyone's here.

23:27.020 --> 23:28.460
Right turn!

23:29.120 --> 23:30.860
March!

23:30.900 --> 23:32.820
One-two-one!

23:32.860 --> 23:34.240
One-two-one!

23:34.740 --> 23:36.260
- Sir.
- Speak.

23:37.040 --> 23:39.720
I think I've got heatstroke.
I'm really dizzy.

23:39.760 --> 23:40.620
Step out.

23:43.140 --> 23:44.580
Eyes forward. Chin up.

23:45.080 --> 23:46.120
Eyes right!

23:47.860 --> 23:49.360
- Sir.
- Speak.

23:49.400 --> 23:50.800
I've got a stomachache.

23:51.480 --> 23:52.400
Step out.

23:52.940 --> 23:55.820
Look at you all,
can't even stand straight.

23:56.480 --> 23:58.200
Some of you lie.

23:58.240 --> 24:00.280
Some of you slack off.

24:01.340 --> 24:02.440
But in this group,

24:02.480 --> 24:03.900
we do have a role model.

24:03.940 --> 24:06.240
Like Lin Qile.

24:06.800 --> 24:08.360
Tiny little girl like her,

24:08.400 --> 24:09.880
but she's held her ground

24:09.920 --> 24:11.140
since day one.

24:11.640 --> 24:13.460
That's the spirit you should all
be learning from.

24:14.360 --> 24:15.220
Chin up, chest out!

24:34.460 --> 24:35.440
We're here.

24:36.200 --> 24:37.760
Finally made it back.

24:45.380 --> 24:46.420
Bye!

24:48.780 --> 24:49.680
Bye!

25:00.640 --> 25:02.480
…wouldn't want a roommate like that.

25:04.280 --> 25:06.100
Then do something about it.

26:07.420 --> 26:08.560
Ugh, I'm bored.

26:08.600 --> 26:09.820
Tell us a ghost story?

26:11.840 --> 26:12.940
Seriously?

26:13.560 --> 26:14.400
You're not scared?

26:16.240 --> 26:17.540
Junior Lin, hey.

26:17.580 --> 26:19.100
Wanna join us?

26:21.520 --> 26:22.860
Sure, I'll listen.

26:27.500 --> 26:28.620
So

26:29.740 --> 26:31.040
have you heard about

26:31.900 --> 26:36.080
that dorm at the end of the hallway?

26:36.120 --> 26:37.640
The end of the hall?

26:38.260 --> 26:39.680
This room is at the end of the hall.

26:39.720 --> 26:40.740
What's the story?

26:40.780 --> 26:42.240
You've never heard?

26:43.320 --> 26:45.400
It's a true story.

26:45.440 --> 26:47.460
Happened

26:47.500 --> 26:49.360
maybe ten years ago.

26:50.740 --> 26:53.740
No one was ever allowed to live

26:54.240 --> 26:55.900
in the dorm at the very end.

26:55.940 --> 26:57.720
Door always locked.

26:58.520 --> 27:01.120
Professors said it was
just a storage room.

27:01.160 --> 27:02.160
So it was summer break.

27:02.200 --> 27:07.360
A girl named Xiaohong didn't go home
because her family was struggling.

27:07.400 --> 27:09.440
She stayed on campus

27:09.480 --> 27:11.700
to work part-time and study.

27:12.300 --> 27:14.000
One rainy night,

27:14.040 --> 27:16.700
she came back to the dorm

27:17.520 --> 27:21.480
and noticed the light was on

27:22.060 --> 27:23.540
in that end room.

27:25.680 --> 27:26.540
She thought,

27:27.280 --> 27:28.720
"That's weird.

27:28.760 --> 27:31.780
No one's supposed to be living there."

27:31.820 --> 27:35.300
She slowly walked over.

27:43.140 --> 27:44.160
Peeked through the door

27:44.760 --> 27:45.760
and saw a mirror

27:46.380 --> 27:48.500
facing directly at her.

27:48.540 --> 27:51.140
But what she saw in the reflection
wasn't her face!

27:51.180 --> 27:53.940
It was someone else. Only a meter tall.

27:53.980 --> 27:56.400
Only an upper body!

27:57.020 --> 27:57.960
Turns out

27:58.920 --> 28:01.120
she'd been cut in half.

28:09.100 --> 28:10.300
So creepy.

28:10.980 --> 28:12.540
- Yeah.
- Junior Lin,

28:13.260 --> 28:14.460
aren't you scared?

28:15.480 --> 28:17.840
I'm alright.

28:20.240 --> 28:22.240
Why, do you want me to be?

28:23.760 --> 28:24.980
So you're not scared?

28:27.040 --> 28:28.720
You just don't look like the brave type.

28:31.600 --> 28:32.980
Actually,

28:33.020 --> 28:34.480
I know a ghost story too.

28:34.520 --> 28:35.520
Wanna hear it?

28:41.400 --> 28:43.420
Ever heard the story

28:44.600 --> 28:46.460
of two best friends, back to back?

28:48.700 --> 28:50.500
There were these two girls,
Qiqi and Yueyue.

28:51.440 --> 28:54.160
They were roommates,

28:54.200 --> 28:55.400
close as sisters.

28:56.640 --> 28:58.480
They shared a bunk bed,

28:58.520 --> 29:02.080
and every night they'd stay up talking.

29:02.620 --> 29:03.620
One night,

29:04.120 --> 29:05.800
they started chatting about something

29:05.840 --> 29:09.360
that happened at school on the 15th day
of the seventh lunar month.

29:10.420 --> 29:12.860
Legend says that one year,
on that exact day,

29:12.900 --> 29:14.980
a pair of best friends

29:15.020 --> 29:18.360
got into a fight over something small
and ended up killing each other.

29:18.400 --> 29:21.440
Ever since then,
people say you can still hear them arguing

29:22.140 --> 29:23.720
in the dorm halls on the 15th day

29:23.760 --> 29:25.760
of the seventh lunar month every year.

29:26.640 --> 29:28.680
So Qiqi and Yueyue made a plan.

29:28.720 --> 29:31.160
This year, they were
going to that building

29:31.200 --> 29:33.400
to see for themselves.

29:34.120 --> 29:35.260
But

29:35.300 --> 29:37.620
just a few days before the 15th,

29:38.540 --> 29:41.240
Yueyue vanished.

29:42.620 --> 29:46.220
Qiqi waited… and waited.

29:46.260 --> 29:48.580
She stayed up till midnight,

29:49.220 --> 29:50.840
but Yueyue never came back.

29:51.740 --> 29:53.220
Suddenly, the phone rang.

29:53.260 --> 29:55.200
There was no voice on the other end.

29:55.960 --> 29:57.160
Qiqi said,

29:58.260 --> 29:59.420
"Hello, Yueyue?

29:59.920 --> 30:01.720
Say something. Yueyue?"

30:03.620 --> 30:06.300
Finally, a soft voice came through,

30:09.440 --> 30:12.260
"I'm… so cold."

30:14.960 --> 30:17.000
Qiqi thought it was a prank

30:17.040 --> 30:18.120
and hung up.

30:18.620 --> 30:21.480
But the next night, right at midnight,

30:22.280 --> 30:24.160
Yueyue called again,

30:25.980 --> 30:27.920
"I'm so cold."

30:30.680 --> 30:32.060
Third night. Same call.

30:32.980 --> 30:34.080
Fourth night. Still cold.

30:34.580 --> 30:36.440
It went on and on until the seventh day,

30:37.860 --> 30:39.520
the 15th.

30:40.640 --> 30:42.320
Yueyue called one more time.

30:43.240 --> 30:45.080
Qiqi couldn't take it anymore.

30:45.120 --> 30:47.120
"Come back." She said.

30:47.160 --> 30:48.820
"Stop messing with me!"

30:49.580 --> 30:51.260
But then Yueyue whispered,

30:51.900 --> 30:53.920
"I never left.

30:54.420 --> 30:57.180
We're best friends, remember?
Back to back."

30:57.220 --> 30:59.240
Qiqi panicked.

30:59.280 --> 31:01.180
She ducked under the covers.

31:02.200 --> 31:03.880
But she couldn't sleep.

31:03.920 --> 31:05.460
She kept tossing and turning.

31:06.360 --> 31:07.960
Finally, she rolled over

31:09.020 --> 31:11.060
and saw Yueyue.

31:11.100 --> 31:12.940
But it wasn't her.

31:12.980 --> 31:16.980
It was her skin.

31:17.660 --> 31:20.140
And just then,
a voice whispered in her ear,

31:20.820 --> 31:22.140
"See?

31:22.180 --> 31:24.120
I told you I was here.

31:25.040 --> 31:28.240
Best friends… back to back.

31:28.280 --> 31:29.400
My dear best friend…

31:31.800 --> 31:33.800
Look at me."

31:44.260 --> 31:47.900
Junior Lin, that was
actually a pretty good story.

31:47.940 --> 31:49.140
Better than mine.

31:49.640 --> 31:52.260
I'm stealing that for my boyfriend.

31:52.760 --> 31:53.640
I'm going to sleep.

31:53.680 --> 31:54.620
We should all sleep.

31:55.120 --> 31:58.100
I've heard too many of these.
Kinda boring now.

31:58.140 --> 32:00.580
Yeah, we… um, we've got class tomorrow.

32:11.660 --> 32:14.240
Today was my first night in the new dorm.

32:14.280 --> 32:15.140
SEND TO JIANG QIAOXI

32:15.180 --> 32:17.820
But the senior girls
all tried to scare me off.

32:18.580 --> 32:20.700
They told ghost stories
to get me to leave.

32:21.520 --> 32:22.740
I wasn't scared.

32:23.700 --> 32:24.900
I scared them back.

32:26.440 --> 32:27.620
Jiang Qiaoxi,

32:28.700 --> 32:29.960
how have you been?

32:31.100 --> 32:32.360
Are the people around you

32:32.900 --> 32:34.020
treating you well?

33:02.440 --> 33:03.760
What are you doing?

33:05.480 --> 33:07.480
I want her to come
to the bathroom with me.

33:09.340 --> 33:12.560
Junior Lin, come pee with me?

33:13.380 --> 33:14.240
What's happening?

33:14.280 --> 33:15.560
Bathroom, please?

33:23.700 --> 33:24.960
It's fine.

33:30.900 --> 33:32.160
You're fine, senior.

33:41.920 --> 33:43.000
How far is it?

33:44.060 --> 33:46.720
Hurry up, come on. One, two, three.

33:49.360 --> 33:51.220
Nope! That's not it!

33:51.260 --> 33:52.240
That made me jump.

33:52.800 --> 33:54.060
Though someone was there.

33:55.960 --> 33:56.940
Come on.

34:06.660 --> 34:08.260
Junior Lin, hey.

34:08.300 --> 34:09.400
Why don't we share

34:09.900 --> 34:10.800
the same bed tonight?

34:18.179 --> 34:20.120
I mean, I guess that's fine.

34:22.020 --> 34:22.900
There's room.

34:33.920 --> 34:37.480
You were totally freaked out, weren't you?

34:39.020 --> 34:40.219
I was alright.

34:40.920 --> 34:42.080
But seriously,

34:42.659 --> 34:45.940
you don't get scared
telling ghost stories?

34:49.139 --> 34:51.219
Actually, I have a magic spell.

34:52.760 --> 34:53.739
A spell?

34:58.920 --> 35:00.380
"Ghost, ghost,

35:00.880 --> 35:02.640
if you're here,

35:02.680 --> 35:04.000
can you turn on the light for me?"

35:06.400 --> 35:08.120
What kind of spell is that?

35:08.160 --> 35:09.180
Is it a summoning spell?

35:09.920 --> 35:12.240
Look,

35:12.280 --> 35:15.200
if the ghost turns on the light,

35:15.240 --> 35:17.340
that means it's a friendly ghost.

35:17.380 --> 35:18.600
It won't hurt you.

35:19.100 --> 35:20.880
If it doesn't,

35:20.920 --> 35:22.920
then it's a weak ghost with no powers,

35:22.960 --> 35:24.040
and still won't hurt you.

35:25.880 --> 35:28.000
Where did you even hear that?

35:28.540 --> 35:29.840
My dad told me.

35:31.120 --> 35:32.500
It's just something

35:33.340 --> 35:34.560
to comfort you mentally.

35:35.400 --> 35:37.660
And your fear of ghost is pure mentally.

35:38.220 --> 35:40.300
There's no such thing anyway.

35:44.220 --> 35:45.640
That kind of makes sense.

35:46.140 --> 35:47.380
Let me try.

35:47.920 --> 35:48.820
"Ghost,

35:49.960 --> 35:51.320
if you're really here,

35:51.360 --> 35:53.140
turn the light on for me."

35:58.240 --> 35:59.580
What are you two doing

35:59.620 --> 36:01.240
sharing one bed?

36:01.900 --> 36:03.660
- I am scared…
- In the middle of the night

36:03.700 --> 36:05.700
and you're chatting with ghosts?

36:05.740 --> 36:09.900
Who was that talking to me?

36:11.480 --> 36:12.520
Get up.

36:13.160 --> 36:14.760
Bunch of scaredy-cats trying to

36:14.800 --> 36:16.800
freak someone out,
then scaring ourselves instead.

36:16.840 --> 36:18.000
Unbelievable.

36:22.740 --> 36:24.100
Seniors,

36:25.420 --> 36:27.340
I guess I owe you an apology

36:27.380 --> 36:29.020
for scaring you back.

36:29.780 --> 36:31.360
But you started it,

36:31.400 --> 36:33.760
telling ghost stories to freak me out.

36:34.960 --> 36:36.000
See?

36:36.040 --> 36:38.600
Look at this kid, holding a grudge.

36:39.460 --> 36:41.760
So we scared you,
and you just had to scare us back?

36:41.800 --> 36:44.400
I just wanted to show you
I'm not easy to push around.

36:45.160 --> 36:46.940
You can't get rid of me that easily.

36:46.980 --> 36:47.880
Get rid of you?

36:47.920 --> 36:50.000
Why would we want to do that?

36:50.040 --> 36:51.020
Yeah.

36:51.060 --> 36:52.760
You're cute. You're fun.

36:53.300 --> 36:55.480
We adore you. Why would we kick you out?

36:55.520 --> 36:56.980
How could you…

36:58.760 --> 36:59.920
I heard everything.

37:03.200 --> 37:04.840
I was standing outside the door.

37:04.880 --> 37:06.980
You said you didn't like
roommates like me.

37:07.020 --> 37:08.920
Said you didn't want to live with me.

37:08.960 --> 37:11.000
Said you'd find a way to make me leave.

37:11.540 --> 37:14.220
I was so scared,
I didn't even dare come back.

37:14.260 --> 37:16.360
I sat downstairs by myself
until the doors locked.

37:16.400 --> 37:19.060
I only came up
because I thought you were all asleep.

37:19.100 --> 37:19.940
The moment I laid down,

37:19.980 --> 37:21.780
you started telling ghost stories
to scare me.

37:23.360 --> 37:24.960
What's so funny?

37:25.000 --> 37:26.140
See?

37:26.180 --> 37:29.880
That's why taking things
out of context is dangerous.

37:30.380 --> 37:33.240
Is freshman bootcamp ending today?

37:34.300 --> 37:36.280
Is that Lin girl coming back?

37:37.700 --> 37:39.140
I'm telling you,

37:39.180 --> 37:42.080
we should never have been
that loud the other day.

37:42.120 --> 37:44.140
We probably scared her half to death.

37:45.840 --> 37:48.100
None of us were sober, though.

37:48.140 --> 37:49.540
Stupid booze ruined everything.

37:51.280 --> 37:53.640
She seemed so quiet and polite.

37:53.680 --> 37:55.820
What if she's really afraid of us now?

37:57.560 --> 37:58.780
Is she thinking of changing rooms?

37:59.320 --> 38:00.860
Wouldn't be that surprising if she did.

38:02.140 --> 38:02.980
If I were her,

38:03.020 --> 38:04.740
I wouldn't want roommates like us.

38:06.020 --> 38:08.380
Then do something about it.

38:09.940 --> 38:11.420
Wanna try something that hits her

38:11.460 --> 38:12.300
right in the feels?

38:12.340 --> 38:13.700
How?

38:13.740 --> 38:15.200
"Misattribution of arousal,

38:15.240 --> 38:18.060
also known as the
Capilano Suspension Bridge Effect,

38:18.100 --> 38:19.320
is a psychological phenomenon."

38:19.860 --> 38:20.820
Basically,

38:20.860 --> 38:21.960
when someone goes through

38:22.000 --> 38:23.480
intense emotions,

38:23.520 --> 38:25.680
like fear or excitement

38:25.720 --> 38:28.380
their heart starts racing,
blood pressure rises,

38:28.420 --> 38:30.300
they breathe faster.

38:30.340 --> 38:32.700
All those physical reactions

38:32.740 --> 38:34.620
can get misread as romantic attraction

38:34.660 --> 38:38.340
to whoever's with them in that moment.

38:38.380 --> 38:39.720
Oh, that's easy.

38:41.020 --> 38:42.640
We just tell her a scary ghost story.

38:43.160 --> 38:44.920
Once her heart's pounding

38:44.960 --> 38:46.220
and she's all worked up,

38:46.720 --> 38:47.840
Meng Lijun,

38:47.880 --> 38:49.420
you swoop in like a caring senior

38:50.060 --> 38:51.820
and let her sleep in your bed.

38:51.860 --> 38:53.560
And then,

38:53.600 --> 38:55.340
after one night together,

38:55.380 --> 38:56.780
boom, bond formed.

38:58.060 --> 38:59.920
You guys are unbelievable.

38:59.960 --> 39:00.900
You…

39:00.940 --> 39:04.400
You guys are seniors. Seniors!
And you're still this childish?

39:04.440 --> 39:05.440
So what?

39:08.560 --> 39:11.420
You're actually kinda sweet though.

39:11.460 --> 39:13.060
Thought we were trying to kick you out,

39:13.100 --> 39:14.920
and you still walked me to the bathroom.

39:14.960 --> 39:16.600
Even shared your bed with me.

39:19.620 --> 39:20.580
Senior,

39:21.500 --> 39:22.600
so,

39:22.640 --> 39:23.520
do you like me?

39:25.800 --> 39:26.940
Do you like me?

39:28.680 --> 39:30.320
I feel like you kinda do.

39:31.980 --> 39:34.020
Guess that bridge effect thing

39:34.060 --> 39:35.440
might be onto something after all.

39:35.480 --> 39:36.460
Right?

39:37.360 --> 39:38.560
Right, right.

39:38.600 --> 39:40.240
Makes sense. I'm telling you.

39:40.280 --> 39:42.420
Next time I'm dating someone,

39:42.460 --> 39:43.560
I'm using this trick.

39:44.440 --> 39:46.360
- Totally foolproof.
- Guaranteed to work.

39:46.400 --> 39:47.480
Seriously.

40:04.760 --> 40:05.800
Yingtao, look.

40:06.400 --> 40:07.600
Another nightly performance.

40:08.100 --> 40:09.340
It's louder

40:09.380 --> 40:11.020
than the Spring Festival Gala in here.

40:14.300 --> 40:15.280
Come on.

40:16.200 --> 40:17.360
- What?
- Come on.

40:17.860 --> 40:19.900
Lijun, can you call Sisi for me?

40:20.660 --> 40:22.400
Boys aren't allowed in the girls' dorm.

40:27.680 --> 40:30.420
Lijun, um…

40:30.460 --> 40:32.000
He's not here for me.

40:33.480 --> 40:34.780
Then for who?

40:34.820 --> 40:37.300
That's Sisi's boyfriend, Shi Zhan.

40:37.800 --> 40:39.800
Oh, they had a fight?

40:39.840 --> 40:41.300
He came to apologize?

40:42.200 --> 40:43.360
It's not that simple.

40:43.400 --> 40:44.980
They're both seniors.

40:45.660 --> 40:49.180
Shi Zhan wants to move back to Shandong
and get a public school teaching job.

40:49.220 --> 40:50.260
But Sisi

40:50.300 --> 40:53.060
is going back to Suzhou
to try for a civil service job.

40:53.100 --> 40:56.160
Shi Zhan wants her
to go with him, get married.

40:56.200 --> 40:58.220
Sisi wants to break up.

41:02.640 --> 41:03.540
WOMEN'S DORM MEN KEEP OUT

41:03.580 --> 41:06.260
She never mentioned this.

41:06.300 --> 41:09.040
She doesn't want to.
And we're not gonna push her.

41:10.300 --> 41:12.620
Remember the day you arrived,
when we were all hungover?

41:13.120 --> 41:14.500
We were talking about it the night.

41:27.480 --> 41:28.520
Is he still downstairs?

41:32.900 --> 41:33.940
Yeah.

41:50.640 --> 41:51.660
Sisi.

42:06.020 --> 42:07.280
Sisi!

42:08.340 --> 42:10.140
What are you doing?

42:12.280 --> 42:14.060
A relationship takes two people.

42:14.560 --> 42:17.180
You can't just decide everything
on your own.

42:18.240 --> 42:19.260
Sisi!

42:20.280 --> 42:22.260
Is this it?

42:23.540 --> 42:24.800
Yeah.

42:34.640 --> 42:35.760
It's fine. I…

42:36.800 --> 42:37.860
I told him…

42:40.400 --> 42:43.160
Told him not to stand there
getting all emotional by himself.

42:43.700 --> 42:46.120
Honestly, I knew from the start

42:47.460 --> 42:48.980
we'd break up after graduation.

42:50.340 --> 42:52.460
It just happened
a year earlier than expected.

42:59.460 --> 43:01.180
You guys go do your thing.

43:01.220 --> 43:02.200
I…

43:02.860 --> 43:04.440
I just need a minute alone.

43:11.820 --> 43:13.700
Yingtao, get changed.

43:13.740 --> 43:15.000
The showers close soon.

45:42.360 --> 45:44.640
Subtitle translation by: Jiaxin Wang
